costa
------------------------------------------
COSTA is a communication-optimal, highly-optimised algorithm for data
redistribution accross multiple processors, using MPI and OpenMP and offering
the possibility to transpose and scale some or all data.

Runtime requirements:
  cygwin-3.6.10-1
  libcosta-devel-2.3.2-1bl1
  libcosta2-2.3.2-1bl1
  libgcc1-14.4.0-1
  libgomp1-14.4.0-1
  libopenmpi40-4.1.6-1
  libscalapack2.2-2.2.2-1bl1
  libstdc++6-14.4.0-1
  pkg-config-3.0.4-2

Build requirements:
(besides corresponding -devel packages)
  binutils-2.47-1
  cmake-4.2.1-1
  cygport-0.37.7-1
  gcc-core-14.4.0-1
  gcc-g++-14.4.0-1
  libopenmpi-devel-4.1.6-1
  libscalapack-devel-2.2.2-1bl1
  ninja-1.13.2-1

Canonical website:
  https://github.com/eth-cscs/COSTA

Canonical download:
  https://github.com/eth-cscs/COSTA/archive/refs/tags/v2.3.2.tar.gz

-------------------------------------------

Build instructions:
  1. unpack costa-2.3.2-X-src.tar.xz
  2. if you use setup to install this src package,
     it will be unpacked under /usr/src automatically
        % cd /usr/src
        % cygport ./costa-2.3.2-X.cygport all

This will create:
  /usr/src/costa-2.3.2-X-src.tar.xz
  /usr/src/costa-2.3.2-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libcosta2-2.3.2-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libcosta-devel-2.3.2-X.tar.xz

